{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CghAUaZu2VYEVYv6QFNTW", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The architecture graph doesn't say how often RenewalsWorker re-bills subscriptions. I couldn't find a schedule, interval or retry setting for it.\n\n**What the graph does record:**\n\n- **Configuration:** RenewalsWorker has one configuration key, **AUTH_HOLD_MINUTES**. It \"sets how long a renewal authorization is held before capture.\" That's how long a payment hold lasts before the charge is collected. It's not how often renewals run, so it doesn't answer your question.\n- **What RenewalsWorker needs to run:**\n  - It depends on **BillingService**. BillingService stores data in **BillingPostgresDatabase**, calls **NotificationsAPI** (served by **NotificationsService**), and depends on **OrderService**.\n  - It calls **PaymentsAPI**, which is served by **PaymentsService**. PaymentsService stores data in **PaymentsPostgresDatabase** and is configured by **PAYMENT_API_KEY** and **CAPTURE_TIMEOUT**.\n- **Other places I checked:** BillingService has no configuration keys recorded. PaymentsService's two keys cover the API key and the capture timeout, not how often billing happens.\n\nThe frequency is probably set somewhere the graph doesn't cover, such as a cron or scheduler definition, a deployment manifest, or a constant in RenewalsWorker's code. Look there next."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 194, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5491, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 194}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "987dacce-b45a-4f5a-8ffb-dbd898e5ddac", "uuid": "